  "textContent": "The first day of rehearsals for the television special James Paul McCartney took place on 22 February 1973. Rehearsals and filming took place at Elstree Studios. On this day Wings were in the studio to rehearse their concert sequence, which was filmed on 18 March. The rehearsals were filmed, and the audio was used for the final soundtrack.Produced by ATV, James Paul McCartney was first broadcast on 16 April 1973 in the USA, and 10 May in the UK. It was released on DVD as part of the super deluxe reissue of in Red Rose Speedway December 2018.\n\n\n\n\n\nPage last updated: 28 November 2025Also on this day...2015: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Coliseo de Puerto Rico, San Juan1999: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Value City Arena, Columbus1994: US album release: Strawberries Oceans Ships Forest by The Fireman (Paul McCartney and Youth)1993: Paul McCartney live: Festhalle, Frankfurt1975: Tape copying: Venus And Mars by Wings1972: Wings live: Swansea University1972: Recording, mixing: Woman Is The N****r Of The World by John Lennon and Yoko Ono1971: Mixing: Power To The People by John Lennon/Plastic Ono Band1971: Paul McCartney’s court hearing to dissolve The Beatles’ partnership – day two1971: Recording: Ram On, Now Hear This Song Of Mine by Paul and Linda McCartney1971: US single release: Another Day by Paul McCartney1970: Recording, mixing: Every Night, That Would Be Something, Valentine Day, Maybe I’m Amazed by Paul McCartney1969: Recording: I Want You (She’s So Heavy)1967: Recording, mixing: A Day In The Life1965: The Beatles fly to the Bahamas to film Help!1964: Interviews: London Airport1963: The Beatles live: Oasis Club, Manchester1963: Northern Songs is formed1961: The Beatles live: Hambleton Hall, Liverpool1961: The Beatles live: Aintree Institute, LiverpoolWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
